/T (4. Scope and Limitations The scope of this research is primarily conceptual and interpretive. It does not rely on empirical data collection such as surveys or interviews; instead, it analyzes texts within their socio-legal and philosophical context. While this approach provides depth in theoretical understanding, it does not empirically measure public responses to legal language. Future research could incorporate empirical linguistics or experimental methods \(e.g., testing how metaphors influence jury decision-making\) to complement the present analysis.)
