/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (This analysis also revealed how globalization reinforces the dominance of English in international law, treaties, and arbitration \(Khan, 2023; Steger, 2013\). While English as a legal lingua franca facilitates efficiency, it also entrenches linguistic inequality, marginalizing speakers of less dominant languages. Thus, the multilingual analysis demonstrated that language in law is both an instrument of inclusion and exclusion, depending on its accessibility.)
