/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (RESEARCH DISCUSSION The findings of this study reinforce the proposition that language is not peripheral but constitutive of law. Through doctrinal, discourse, and metaphorical analysis, it became evident that legal authority is linguistically constructed and sustained. This section discusses the broader implications of these findings, situating them within existing scholarship and identifying avenues for reform and future inquiry.)
/E (RESEARCH DISCUSSION The findings of this study reinforce the proposition that language is not peripheral but constitutive of law. Through doctrinal, discourse, and metaphorical analysis, it became evident that legal authority is linguistically constructed and sustained. This section discusses the broader implications of these findings, situating them within existing scholarship and identifying avenues for reform and future inquiry.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0]
>>
