/T (where English functions as a gatekeeper to legal and economic participation. The findings therefore suggest that multilingualism in law is a double-edged phenomenon: while it offers inclusivity, it also risks reinforcing hierarchies when dominant languages overshadow minority voices.)
/E (where English functions as a gatekeeper to legal and economic participation. The findings therefore suggest that multilingualism in law is a double-edged phenomenon: while it offers inclusivity, it also risks reinforcing hierarchies when dominant languages overshadow minority voices.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
