/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The implications of this study extend beyond theory to practice. For legislators, plain-language drafting and ethical rhetorical choices can reduce opacity and enhance legitimacy. In conclusion, language remains the central medium through which law commands, persuades, and legitimizes. Recognizing the power, risks, and ethical responsibilities embedded in legal language and acknowledging that social obedience itself emerges from the conscious linguistic construction of law is essential to ensuring that law functions not only as a mechanism of authority but also as an instrument of justice, inclusivity, and democratic legitimacy.)
/E (The implications of this study extend beyond theory to practice. For legislators, plain-language drafting and ethical rhetorical choices can reduce opacity and enhance legitimacy. In conclusion, language remains the central medium through which law commands, persuades, and legitimizes. Recognizing the power, risks, and ethical responsibilities embedded in legal language and acknowledging that social obedience itself emerges from the conscious linguistic construction of law is essential to ensuring that law functions not only as a mechanism of authority but also as an instrument of justice, inclusivity, and democratic legitimacy.)
/Pg 18 0 R
